# Cloudflare DNS API token, for Let's Encrypt DNS-01 on media.virgo.ph.
#
# Copy to `cloudflare-dns.ini` NEXT TO docker-compose.prod.yml on the
# production host and fill in the token. That filename is gitignored; this
# example is the only version that belongs in the repository.
#
# DNS-01 rather than HTTP-01 for two reasons. Philippine consumer and some
# business plans block inbound port 80, which would make HTTP-01 fail in a way
# that looks like a firewall problem for a day; and DNS-01 needs no second
# open port on a host whose whole security story is "only 443, only nginx".
#
# This is a DNS API token. It is not the CDN, and media.virgo.ph stays a
# DNS-only record — see docs/MEDIA_DELIVERY.md.
#
# Create at https://dash.cloudflare.com/profile/api-tokens with exactly:
#
#   Permissions:     Zone → DNS → Edit
#   Zone Resources:  Include → Specific zone → virgo.ph
#
# Nothing wider. A token that can edit DNS for every zone on the account is
# not needed here and is a much worse thing to leak.
#
# Certbot warns if this file is group- or world-readable. On Windows that
# check is advisory and it proceeds anyway, so keep the file out of any
# synced or shared folder rather than relying on the warning.

dns_cloudflare_api_token = REPLACE_ME
